2186045443] [17592186518327 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $12{x}^{2}\\cdot {8}^{x-3}+7x\\cdot {8}^{x-3}-49\\cdot {8}^{x-3}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518327 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "687c8f09-08ba-5f3e-a91b-2c278344272b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518327 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{2}\\cdot {8}^{x-3}+7x\\cdot {8}^{x-3}-49\\cdot {8}^{x-3} & =0 \\\\ (12{x}^{2}+7x-49){8}^{x-3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n12{x}^{2}+7x-49=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{8}^{x-3}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $12{x}^{2}+7x-49=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(4x-7)(3x+7)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{7}{3},\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\n- The equation ${8}^{x-3}=0$ has no solutions because ${8}^{x-3}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518332 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518331 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518332 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518332 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the product of solutions of the equation $6{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+19x\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+15\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}=0?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518332 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae55bf0c-c4b6-5b6c-a289-5c5d946d9710" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518332 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+19x\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1}+15\\cdot {4}^{-3x+1} & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}+19x+15){4}^{-3x+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+19x+15=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{4}^{-3x+1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $6{x}^{2}+19x+15=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x+5)(2x+3)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{5}{3},-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- The equation ${4}^{-3x+1}=0$ has no solutions because ${4}^{-3x+1}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-\\frac{5}{3},-\\frac{3}{2},$ and their product is $-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot -\\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518318 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518340 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518333 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $8{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+34x\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+21\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b0e3548f-1fa8-5d7e-a0b1-0803e5136f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518333 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+34x\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2}+21\\cdot {7}^{-2x-2} & =0 \\\\ (8{x}^{2}+34x+21){7}^{-2x-2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n8{x}^{2}+34x+21=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{7}^{-2x-2}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $8{x}^{2}+34x+21=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(4x+3)(2x+7)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n- The equation ${7}^{-2x-2}=0$ has no solutions because ${7}^{-2x-2}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{7}{2}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518336 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518320 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518336 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518324 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518336 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518336 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $9{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{-2x-2}-36x\\cdot {4}^{-2x-2}+35\\cdot {4}^{-2x-2}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518336 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c650cd7c-5bee-5601-bb43-0158a5dccd30" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518336 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{-2x-2}-36x\\cdot {4}^{-2x-2}+35\\cdot {4}^{-2x-2} & =0 \\\\ (9{x}^{2}-36x+35){4}^{-2x-2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}-36x+35=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{4}^{-2x-2}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $9{x}^{2}-36x+35=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(3x-5)(3x-7)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=\\frac{5}{3},\\frac{7}{3}.$\n\n- The equation ${4}^{-2x-2}=0$ has no solutions because ${4}^{-2x-2}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{3}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518342 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518330 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518342 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518341 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518342 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518342 #edb/ref 1071 "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation $8{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{2-x}-14x\\cdot {4}^{2-x}-15\\cdot {4}^{2-x}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518342 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f1568554-8d81-533e-b297-bd3644ea98ef" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518342 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{2-x}-14x\\cdot {4}^{2-x}-15\\cdot {4}^{2-x} & =0 \\\\ (8{x}^{2}-14x-15){4}^{2-x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n8{x}^{2}-14x-15=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{4}^{2-x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $8{x}^{2}-14x-15=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x-5)(4x+3)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-\\frac{3}{4},\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n- The equation ${4}^{2-x}=0$ has no solutions because ${4}^{2-x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{and}\\,x=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518345 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186157437.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518345 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "582cd571-9b10-5256-821d-5ca7caa2b6c2" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1045 "The Power Rule for Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186519665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518981 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8d6616d8-4bd9-5180-836d-7a649de8f37f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518988 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518988 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186519651 #edb/ref 17592